# Source manifest — reproducible-by-reference (Invariant 3).
# Re-clone at build time; the working tree under sources/hk/ is gitignored.
#
# TOOLCHAIN SOURCE — a tool this repo actually RUNS (#81, ingested 2026-08-02).
#
# ⚠️ INVARIANT: this pin MUST track the version we actually run.
#   version source: mise.toml `[tools] hk`
#   pinned here:    1.56.0
# A pin that drifts from the installed version makes the corpus answer questions
# about code we are not running. Not hypothetical — `sources/graphify.manifest`
# records exactly that failure: it sat two releases behind for weeks, so every
# "how does graphify work?" answer came from the wrong source.
#
# Pin the RELEASE TAG, never a branch head — a branch drifts ahead of the release.
# To bump: change the version in its source above, resolve the tag to its COMMIT,
# set ref/commit here to match, then `mise run kb-build`:
#   gh api repos/jdx/hk/commits/<tag> --jq .sha
#
# ⚠️ NOT `git ls-remote --tags <url> <tag>` (#395), which is what this line said
# until 2026-08-19. Naming the tag EXACTLY is what makes it wrong: the commit an
# annotated tag points at is on the peeled `<tag>^{}` line, and an exact pattern
# does not match that line, so only the tag object comes back. Control-armed
# against jdx/mise v2026.8.8 on 2026-08-20 — exact pattern returns one line
# (`ca93e5fe…`, the tag object) with or WITHOUT `--refs`, while the glob
# `'v2026.8.8*'` returns both and `--refs` then suppresses the useful one. So
# neither adding `--refs` nor dropping it rescues the exact form.
# hk happens to ship LIGHTWEIGHT tags, so that call returned the
# commit here and this file was never wrong — but the identical instruction in
# `sources/mise.manifest` put a TAG OBJECT in its `commit` field for 17 days,
# because mise ships annotated ones. The instruction was the defect; that it did
# not fire here is luck, not safety, and hk could switch tag styles tomorrow.
#
# kind = code: AST extraction only, no LLM, no cost. NOTE this extracts the
# SOURCE and skips every .md by design — the tool's DOCS are a separate
# `kind = docs` mirror (#123), not this manifest.
url = https://github.com/jdx/hk
ref = v1.56.0
commit = bad550709d9ce2e6f43a8d25880e1c7d6397f13f
kind = code
added = 2026-08-02
